---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import InputOTPDemo from "../../components/InputOTPDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Input OTP"
  description="A one-time code field with one slot per character."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Input OTP</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A one-time code field for sign-in and verification codes. Each character
    gets its own slot, and slots can be split into groups such as
    <code>123–456</code>.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><InputOTPDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Input OTP usage"
      code={`import {
  InputOTP,
  InputOTPGroup,
  InputOTPSeparator,
  InputOTPSlot,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/input-otp";

const [code, setCode] = useState("194278");
const [showError, setShowError] = useState(true);

<InputOTP
  maxLength={6}
  value={code}
  onChange={(value) => {
    setCode(value);
    setShowError(false);
  }}
  aria-label="Verification code"
  aria-invalid={showError}
  aria-describedby="otp-error"
>
  <InputOTPGroup>
    <InputOTPSlot index={0} />
    <InputOTPSlot index={1} />
    <InputOTPSlot index={2} />
  </InputOTPGroup>
  <InputOTPSeparator />
  <InputOTPGroup>
    <InputOTPSlot index={3} />
    <InputOTPSlot index={4} />
    <InputOTPSlot index={5} />
  </InputOTPGroup>
</InputOTP>
<p id="otp-error" role="alert">That code didn’t match. Try again.</p>`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Parts</h2>
    <p>
      <code>InputOTP</code> is built on Base UI <code>OTPField.Root</code>.
      <code>maxLength</code> sets the number of slots. Use
      <code>defaultValue</code> for an uncontrolled code, or
      <code>value</code> with <code>onChange(value)</code> to control it.
      <code>onValueChange</code>, <code>onValueComplete</code>,
      <code>disabled</code>, <code>readOnly</code>, <code>required</code>,
      <code>name</code>, <code>mask</code>, and <code>autoSubmit</code> pass through
      to Base UI. Codes are numeric by default; set
      <code>validationType="alphanumeric"</code> for letters.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>InputOTPGroup</code> joins its slots into one bordered segment with rounded
      outer corners. <code>InputOTPSlot</code> is a real input; pass its zero-based
      <code>index</code> and render slots in order.
      <code>InputOTPSeparator</code> draws a dash between groups.
    </p>
    <p>
      Slots are 32px square with 14px text. On coarse pointers they grow to 44px
      with 16px text so each slot is an easy touch target. Groups sit 8px apart.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">States</h2>
    <p>
      The focused slot gets a focus border and a soft 2px ring above its
      neighbors. <code>aria-invalid</code> on <code>InputOTP</code> marks every slot
      invalid; you can also set it per slot. Invalid slots draw a danger border, and
      their group gets a faint danger ring. Point
      <code>aria-describedby</code> at the error text.
      <code>disabled</code> dims the field to 50% and blocks edits.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Keyboard and accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Typing moves to the next slot. Backspace clears and moves back; Delete
      clears in place. Arrow keys move between slots, and Home and End jump to
      the first slot and the last filled one. Paste or one-time-code autofill
      fills every slot at once. Only the active slot is in the tab order.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>aria-label</code> names the field and its first slot; later slots are
      announced as “Character 2 of 6”. Alternatively, pass
      <code>id</code> and use a <code>Label htmlFor</code>. Color changes take
      120ms and stop when reduced motion is requested. In forced colors mode
      slots keep a system border and a highlight focus ring.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Slot borders use <code>--sprout-input</code>, the fill
      <code>--sprout-surface</code>, text <code>--sprout-text</code>, and the
      separator <code>--sprout-muted</code>. Focus uses
      <code>--sprout-focus</code> and invalid <code>--sprout-danger</code>.
      Outer corners follow <code>--sprout-radius-control</code>. The opt-in
      TulipFarm theme tints the focus ring through these tokens.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
